Host-ABI crash fix for GCC 2.7.2's reorg.c: declare negate_rtx.

Adopted 2026-08-24 (owner ruling 262930f1b, adoption fea9fa2ac;
docs/grind/decisions.md 2026-08-24 "cc1 fork-crash fix"). It has been in the
operative build/cc1 since then. It was pinned as a tracked recipe input on
2026-09-25 under owner ruling bcdc1648e (docs/ORACLE-COMPILER.md, ruling item
(E)1), because the recipe applied only the PLUS->IOR patch. A rebuild "from
the recipe" would otherwise have silently dropped the approved fix.

negate_rtx is declared only in expr.h, which reorg.c does not include. On a
64-bit host the K&R implicit declaration truncates the returned rtx pointer to
32 bits, and cc1 crashes in fill_slots_from_thread. The 32-bit original
cc1psx never crashed. Codegen is unchanged wherever the unfixed compiler
survives, and the full-build SHA1 pins it.

This hunk reproduces byte-for-byte the block present in the live
tools/gcc-2.7.2/reorg.c. Removing exactly that block from the live file gives
the pre-crash-fix manifest hash 73a15a5245d2e7ad55fa9e3c42d724488b1892d6. It
adds nothing else. Applied by tools/build_oracle_cc1.sh to the pinned
upstream 43d1cdb67ed135879869b5266f01efaaada5e35a.

Since owner ruling 2026-09-26 Q17 ("consider a compiler patch a cheat";
.claude/rules/no-compiler-divergence.md) this is the ONLY patch the recipe
applies: the PLUS->IOR patch named above is retired. It is kept as the one
named host-build fix, the author's reading of Q17 and open for the owner to
overrule.

diff --git a/reorg.c b/reorg.c
--- a/reorg.c
+++ b/reorg.c
@@ -130,6 +130,15 @@
 #include "obstack.h"
 #include "insn-attr.h"
 
+/* BB2 crash fix 2026-08-24 (owner ruling, decisions.md "cc1 fork-crash fix"):
+   negate_rtx is declared only in expr.h, which this file does not include.
+   On a 64-bit host the K&R implicit declaration truncates the returned rtx
+   pointer to 32 bits, and the garbage operand SIGSEGVs insn-recog via
+   arith_operand (fill_slots_from_thread increment-compensation path,
+   line ~3646). One-line acceptance fix; codegen pinned by the full-build
+   SHA1 oracle. */
+extern rtx negate_rtx PROTO((enum machine_mode, rtx));
+
 #ifdef DELAY_SLOTS
 
 #define obstack_chunk_alloc xmalloc
